application/pdf; \nGlobal State of Pet Care\r\nStats, Facts and TrendsContents\r\nGlobal Trends in the Pet Population������������������������� 3\r\nPet Ownership������������������������������������������������������������������������������������ 5\r\n How many pets are there in the world?����������������������������5\r\n How many people own a pet?������������������������������������������������6\r\nPet Population Growth ���������������������������������������������������������������� 7\r\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nExchanging Memorandum of Understanding Between UPM and NUS Paves the Way for Revolutionary Companion Animal Cancer Treatment. (https://vet.upm.edu.my/berita/exchanging_memorandum_of_understanding_between_upm_and_nus_paves_the_way_for_revolutionary_companion_animal_cancer_treatment-76111?L=en)\n【turn1234search0】 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.0 years ago; Crawled: last month; \nSerdang, October 27, 2023 - Universiti Putra Malaysia (UPM) and the National University of Singapore (NUS) are embarking on a strategic collaboration that promises to revolutionize the field of anti-cancer therapy. This partnership in brings together two distinguished research teams from the Faculty of Veterinary Medicine, UPM and Yong Loo Lin School of Medicine, NUS to evaluate stem cell therapy for pet dogs and cats with naturally occurring cancers which are good models for comparative oncology.\n\nThe collaboration was marked by the exchanging ceremony of a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on Friday, 27^{th} of October 2023, at the Canselori Putra Building in UPM, a momentous occasion attended by the Vice Chancellor of UPM, Dato’ Professor Dr. Ahmad Farhan Mohd Sadullah, representatives from NUS, Assoc. Prof. Too Heng Phon and Dr Sarah Ho Yoon Khei, along with several distinguished guests, including the Dean of the Faculty of Veterinary Medicine, Prof. Dato’ Dr. Mohd Azmi Mohd Lila, the Deputy Dean (Research and Postgraduate Studies) of the Faculty of Veterinary Medicine, Prof. Dr. Md. Zuki Abu Bakar@Zakaria, the Head of Department for Veterinary Clinical Studies, Assoc. Prof. Dr. Ooi Peck Toung and Assoc. Prof. Dr. Gayathri Thevi Selvarajah.\n\nThe core of this transformative partnership is the refinement of the therapy development and initiation of a clinical trial that focuses on deploying genetically engineered mesenchymal stem cell-based therapy to combat end-stage tumours in companion animals. Cats and dogs with specific types of cancer will soon be recruited into clinical trials through the University Veterinary Hospital of UPM. Associate Professor Dr. Gayathri Thevi Selvarajah, a veterinary oncology specialist will lead the research and clinical trials with the assistance from a research team including surgeons, clinicians, medical laboratory technologists, and pathologist who will work collectively to deliver and manage this innovative therapy for dogs and cats. The goal of this collaboration is to enhance the quality of life and extend the survival of pet cats and dogs diagnosed with selected types of cancer.\n\nThe UPM-NUS partnership is not only poised to transform veterinary medicine but also showcases the power of cross-border collaborations in the pursuit of scientific advancements. As research and development progress, it is anticipated that this novel therapy will soon become standard practice, providing newfound hope to countless pets afflicted with cancer and potentially influencing future treatments for humans.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOncology: Full Veterinary Study Program | ESAVS Asia (https://www.esavs-asia.org/en/study-programs/oncology)\n【turn1234search1】 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; \nOncology I: From “Lump” to Clinical Logic, Cebu/Philippines, Dr. Schmidt & Prof. Selmic  | 05. - 09. Apr 2027  | registration open\nOncology IV: Oncology Case Management (Course 4/5), TBA/China, Dr. Schmidt  | 12. - 16. Apr 2027  | coming soon - Interest List open\nFeline Oncology, Nanjing/China, Dr. Schmidt  | 02. - 06. Aug 2027  | coming soon - Interest List open\nOncology II: Internal & Systemic Tumours, Bangkok/Thailand, Dr. Schmidt & Dr. Janis Lapsley  | 09. - 13. Aug 2027  | registration open\nOncology V, TBA/China, Dr. Schmidt  | 08. - 12. Nov 2027  | coming soon - Interest List open\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nVeterinary Oncology | Advanced Cancer Care for Dogs & Cats (https://www.veshospital.com.sg/services/cancer-care/)\n【turn1234search2】 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9.6 years ago; Crawled: 2 days ago; \nA cancer diagnosis in your pet can feel overwhelming – but just like in human medicine, specialised care can make all the difference. At VES Hospital, Singapore’s only veterinary oncologist offers tailored, advanced and compassionate care to improve your pet’s quality of life.\n\n## Singapore’s Only Veterinary Oncologist\n\nDr Danielle Gibson leads our oncology service with cutting-edge cancer diagnostics and treatments for common cancers in dogs and cats:\nOur multidisciplinary approach ensures your pet receives the most comprehensive cancer care available in Singapore.\n\n## Chemotherapy That Puts Pets First\n\nUnlike in humans, chemotherapy for pets is designed to minimise side effects. Most pets experience little to no discomfort and can continue eating, playing, and enjoying life.\n\nOur oncologist, Dr Danielle Gibson, will be able to offer the following:\n\n  * Personalised Treatment Plans – Tailored chemotherapy protocols for your pet’s specific cancer type.\n  * Effective, Pet-Friendly Treatments – Designed to minimise side effects while ensuring optimal treatment of your pet’s cancer.\n  * Quality of Life for your Pets – Our focus is always on ensuring your pet is happy, comfortable, and pain-free, even while receiving chemotherapy.\nIf your pet has been diagnosed with cancer,  speak to our team today to explore treatment options. Early intervention leads to better outcomes.\n\nCall us +65 6266 0232\n\nHave a question? Please contact us here or call us during hospital hours. We respond within one business day.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCTSG - Your centralised hub for clinical trial information and resources in Singapore. (https://clinicaltrials.sg/)\n【turn1234search3】 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; \n## Singapore’s National Clinical Trials Portal (CTSG)\n\nImage: animated logo\n\nSCRI’s clinical trials portal (CTSG) is your centralised hub for clinical trials information and resources in Singapore. Designed with patients, clinical investigators, and companies in mind, our platform aims to be the go-to solution to meet the diverse needs of the clinical research community.\n\nLearn More\n\nCTSG serves as Singapore Clinical Research Institute’s (SCRI's) centralised portal for all matters pertaining to clinical trials in Singapore, providing comprehensive support and information.\n\nClick below to view the recruiting trials in Singapore.\n\nIf you wish to be notified of new trials in our database, subscribe to receive our new trials alert.\n\nJoin Mailing List Subscribe to New Trials Alert View Recruiting Trials\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCareAcross (https://www.careacross.com/clinical-trials/trial/NCT06144346)\n【turn1234search4】 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; \nName: National Cancer Institute\n\nAddress:\nCity: Cairo\nZip: 11796\nCountry: Egypt\n\nStatus: Recruiting\n\nContact:\nLast name: Rimoun R Boutrus, M.D., Ph.D.\n\nPhone: 00201061056900\nEmail: rimoun.boutrus@nci.cu.edu.eg\nStart date: September 20, 2023\n\nCompletion date: September 20, 2028\n\nLead sponsor:\nAgency: National Cancer Institute, Egypt\nAgency class: Other\n\nSource: National Cancer Institute, Egypt\n\nRecord processing date: ClinicalTrials.gov processed this data on November 12, 2024\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCat Cancer Study | Explore Feline Cancer Treatment Options — Paccal Vet (https://www.paccalvet.com/cat-cancer-study)\n【turn1234search5】 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; \n# Paccal Vet Feline Cancer Trial\n\n### A dose-finding study for cats with solid tumors\n\n  * Fully funded study, no cost to pet owner\n\n  * No placebo, all cats receive active treatment\n\n  * Paccal Vet is based on a cancer drug widely used in human medicine\n\nRECRUITMENT COMPLETED\n\n## Cancer in cats\n\nSolid tumors, including carcinomas, sarcomas, mast cell tumors and lymphomas in cats are often aggressive and can be difficult to treat with currently available treatment options. Despite how common and serious cancer is in cats, there are currently no chemotherapy drugs approved for use in cats.\n\nThis means veterinarians often have to rely on treatments that may not always work as well or be as safe for cats. As more cats live longer and cancer becomes more common, the need for cat-specific cancer treatments is becoming increasingly urgent.\n\n## Why is this study being done?\n\nWe are studying Paccal Vet as a possible new treatment option for cats with solid tumors.\n\nPaccal Vet is a chemotherapy that has been specifically designed for pets, and it is based on a cancer drug that is widely used and approved in human cancer care.\n\nSeveral clinical trials have been performed with Paccal Vet in dogs with promising results, but to date, no studies have evaluated Paccal Vet in cats.  \n\nThe purpose of this study is to test the tolerability of Paccal Vet in cats and to determine an acceptable dose. A secondary, exploratory goal is to see whether Paccal Vet may have anti-cancer activity in various tumors in cats.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nKum Ada Veteriner Onkoloji | Kedi ve Köpeklerde Kanser (https://veterineronkoloji.com/)\n【turn1234search6】 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; \n# Kum Ada Veteriner Onkoloji\n\nKanser tanısı almış ya da kanser şüphesi olan kedi ve köpekler için onkoloji konsültasyonu.\n\nHasta SahibiyimKanser şüphesi ya da tanısı, tedavi süreci ve sık sorulan sorularVeteriner HekimimHasta sevki, makaleler, kemoterapi protokolleri ve vaka sunumları\n\n  * Her gün 09:00–21:00Konsültasyonlar randevu ile yapılır.\n  * Telefon0212 324 67 32\n  * AdresLevent Mah., Çarşı Cad., Sülün Sk. No:14, 34330 Beşiktaş/İstanbul\nKum Ada Veteriner Onkoloji, İstanbul Levent'te kedi ve köpeklerde kanser tanısı ve tedavisine odaklanan bir veteriner onkoloji merkezidir. Kanser tanısı almış ya da kanserden şüphelenilen hastaları, hasta sahipleri ve sevk eden veteriner hekimlerle birlikte değerlendiriyoruz.\n\nHer tedavi kararı; muayene, mevcut tetkik ve raporların değerlendirilmesi ve gerekiyorsa ek tanı ve evreleme çalışmalarından sonra, hayvanınızın kendi durumuna göre verilir. Seçenekler, beklenen faydalar ve olası riskler açıkça konuşulur; karar birlikte verilir.\n\nHasta sahiplerine yönelik bilgilendirici yazılar, veteriner hekimler için makale çevirileri ve özetleri ile vaka sunumları Kütüphane bölümünde yer alır. Bu içerikler genel bilgilendirme amaçlıdır; hayvanınızın durumu için randevu alarak onkolojik değerlendirme yaptırmanız gerekir.\n  * Köpeklerde moleküler hedefli kanser tedavilerinde ikinci dönem 11 Mayıs 2025 Veteriner Hekimler İçin\n  * Kedi primer nonhematopoietik malign karaciğer tümörleri: Çok merkezli retrospektif bir çalışma (2000-2021)4 Mayıs 2025 Veteriner Hekimler İçin\n  * Yüksek grade kutanöz mast hücre tümörlü köpeklere ilişkin klinik sonuçlar 4 Nisan 2025 Veteriner Hekimler İçin\n  * Kedilerde Kutanöz Skuamöz Hücreli Karsinom Tedavisinde Elektrokemoterapi ile Uygulanan Üç Kemoterapi Protokolünün Karşılaştırılması 30 Mart 2025 Veteriner Hekimler İçin\n  * Köpek Hemanjiosarkomunun Moleküler Profili ve Potansiyel Yeni Terapötik Hedefler 2 Mart 2025 Veteriner Hekimler İçin\n\n### Son vaka sunumları\n\n  * DOBERMAN IRKI BİR KÖPEKTE PERİKARDİYAL PRİMER EFÜZYON LENFOMASI 4 Kasım 2024\n  * RETİFORM HEMANJİYOENDOTELİYOM BENZERİ MALİGN KUTANÖZ VASKÜLER TÜMÖRLÜ BİR KÖPEKTE KEMOTERAPİ VE RADYOTERAPİ İLE KOMBİNE TEDAVİ 3 Kasım 2024\n  * BİR KÖPEKTE KEMİĞE İNVAZE SKUAMOZ HÜCRELİ TÜMÖRÜN KLİNİK VE PATOLOJİK DEĞERLENDİRMESİ İLE TEDAVİSİ: VAKA SUNUMU 23 Ocak 2023\n  * MANDİBULADA OSTEOSARKOM TEŞHİSLİ BİR KÖPEĞİN STEREOTAKTİK RADYOTERAPİ İLE TEDAVİSİ OLGU SUNUMU 7 Ocak 2023\n  * Nazal Adenokarsinom Teşhisli Bir Köpekte Kombine Toceranib Fosfat Ve Radyoterapi İle Sağaltımı Olgu Sunumu 2 Ocak 2023"}],"isError":false}}
